348}] :question/id #uuid "a131e90c-6bee-5a11-8f5e-31ad30812f77" :question/math-academy-id "q-8522" :question/problem "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $5$, and that $P$ makes an angle of $330^{∘}$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256389 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48fc86a1-f2ca-5fb6-98bb-2ba50587b6e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3\\sqrt{2},-3\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254297} {:answer/id #uuid "6e2e5dea-eb32-5ef7-b053-292457b74c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254647} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e86342-c856-59b9-acc7-8c16b2779f05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\sqrt{3},-2\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255156} {:answer/id #uuid "bceb10bc-923e-5dff-8dfb-386a60cdb562" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6\\sqrt{2},6\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255360} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3e4f69-01dd-5d42-b6e1-f9b19a563b4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3},-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48fc86a1-f2ca-5fb6-98bb-2ba50587b6e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3\\sqrt{2},-3\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254297} :answer-field/id #uuid "af20ccec-9741-587e-8b2c-0fb701159ee6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256239}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3fe83e25-a491-5f7c-b624-e2aecbbcfc65" :question/math-academy-id "q-120328" :question/problem "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $6,$ and that $P$ makes an angle of ${315}^{∘}$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta )$, where\n\n$$\nr=6,\\,\\theta ={315}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡({315}^{∘}) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{sin}⁡({315}^{∘}) \\\\  & =6(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(3\\sqrt{2},-3\\sqrt{2}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284678 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "753543d7-b063-5cf6-b128-a80a7409bfa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282693} {:answer/id #uuid "76d18bf0-adc0-56ad-a666-eb6830554a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282705} {:answer/id #uuid "9e0cfff2-f165-5112-84b4-84ef6d0d16d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283067} {:answer/id #uuid "b46da797-d4b1-5e93-b5d2-956b71f67813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283252} {:answer/id #uuid "e9302e03-d1d5-5540-a03c-b0e2ce178144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b46da797-d4b1-5e93-b5d2-956b71f67813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283252} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c6099d-d0ba-56c6-9aa9-eadf358e9b15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284002}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f8753c4e-3481-5eda-bb21-d60f3fd06725" :question/math-academy-id "q-17124" :question/problem "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $\\frac{1}{3},$ and that $P$ makes an angle of $\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ where\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6579eacc-068b-5cac-8c3b-3d0005500a11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282560} {:answer/id #uuid "77f0a4c2-79c0-54cd-8fc3-9692d5df1551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\sqrt{2}